Global exception handling: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain5/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` — a `@ControllerAdvice` that produces RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` responses. Its handlers:
- `@ExceptionHandler(AccessDeniedException.class)` → re-throws so Spring Security handles 403.
- `@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)` → 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR (`ERROR_UNEXPECTED`).
- `@ExceptionHandler(DataIntegrityViolationException.class)` → 404 NOT_FOUND (`ERROR_DATA_INTEGRITY`).
- `@ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)` → 400 BAD_REQUEST, populating `schemaValidationErrors`. This is what handles bean-validation failures on the `@Valid` request body (e.g. empty `firstName`, bad `telephone`).

There is currently **no** `@ExceptionHandler` returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`. If you want conflicts raised from the service/repository layer to become 409, you would add a custom exception + handler here.

### 5. Existing tests for owner creation

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain5/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`

